WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.044 --> 00:00:04.544
(bicycle wheels rattling)

00:00:08.861 --> 00:00:11.444
(upbeat music)

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.890
- It's the ocean versus the Dutch.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:22.008
That's the battle that's
going on right now.

00:00:22.008 --> 00:00:23.830
(ticking)

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:25.830
It's been going on for hundreds of years

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.687
and you know, who's winning, the Dutch.

00:00:28.687 --> 00:00:31.354
(upbeat music)

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:34.790
See all that water,

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:37.293
it's super ingenious the
way they designed it.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.030
Can you tell the engineering marvel?

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:42.950
- If I hear one more
thing about the water.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:45.617
(upbeat music)

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:54.270
- Look at this map of Holland in 1300,

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:57.910
compare this to a map of Holland today.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:00.700
The country has gained land.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:04.130
Yes, thousands and thousands
of square kilometers

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:08.459
of land has been won back from the ocean.

00:01:08.459 --> 00:01:09.740
(ticking)

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.530
The story of this battle
between the ocean and the Dutch

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:15.840
explains why Holland is good at cheese,

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.360
why Amsterdam has canals,

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.513
Why Dutch people ride bikes.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:23.180
(upbeat music)

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:28.660
- And for those who are confused,

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:33.020
the Dutch, Netherlands and
Holland are all the same thing

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:34.470
and they all have different reasons

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:35.510
and I'm not gonna go into them.

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:37.290
You can like, look at Wikipedia.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:38.950
This is just when I use those words,

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:41.670
it all has to do with the same
thing, which is this country,

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:42.642
okay?

00:01:42.642 --> 00:01:45.450
(upbeat music)

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:49.120
So the Netherlands or Holland
or whatever you wanna call it

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.410
is a country that is sinking.

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:52.810
It's actually...

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:55.020
the majority of it is under sea level

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.608
or right at sea level.

00:01:56.608 --> 00:01:59.191
(upbeat music)

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:05.440
I mean, if you look at the map of Holland,

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:07.210
you see that a lot of it

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:09.490
is just these little strips of land

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:11.730
that are right up in the North sea

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.650
and the ocean and the wind

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:16.750
just kind of eat away at
this land year after year.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:19.450
Instead of fleeing these
coastal communities

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:22.190
that were slowly sinking into the water,

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:25.572
about 500 years ago, the
Dutch started to fight back.

00:02:25.572 --> 00:02:28.155
(upbeat music)

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.840
Now, let's just be clear about one thing,

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.930
which is, fighting the ocean,

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:40.500
the incessant, timeless
powerhouse, the ocean,

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.160
is a very difficult thing.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:43.173
Where are we going?

00:02:44.077 --> 00:02:45.655
- Texel

00:02:45.655 --> 00:02:46.488
- What?

00:02:46.488 --> 00:02:49.530
(upbeat music)

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:50.363
Texel?

00:02:50.363 --> 00:02:51.448
- Texel.

00:02:51.448 --> 00:02:54.031
(upbeat music)

00:03:22.016 --> 00:03:23.031
- We made it.

00:03:23.031 --> 00:03:23.864
- We made it.

00:03:23.864 --> 00:03:25.960
(upbeat music)

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:30.280
- This battle between the
Netherlands and the ocean

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:32.047
is now much more real for me,

00:03:32.047 --> 00:03:34.730
and this wind and these waves

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:37.890
are so crazy and consistent.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:40.280
They're just eating this land alive

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.660
and yet the Netherlands
have decided to fight back

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.579
and they're doing a pretty darn good job.

00:03:45.579 --> 00:03:48.162
(upbeat music)

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:54.090
- Holland is up for this task.

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:56.130
They've developed a whole system,

00:03:56.130 --> 00:04:00.150
a whole science behind
hydrological engineering

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:01.920
that has allowed them to combat

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.720
the effects and the erosion of the ocean.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.470
- My favorite is the Curry ketchup,

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:09.730
and Johnny loves the (indistinct)

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:12.720
and they actually go really well together.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:13.947
Like us.

00:04:13.947 --> 00:04:16.657
(laughs)

00:04:16.657 --> 00:04:19.240
(upbeat music)

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:22.820
- Okay, so how do they actually do this?

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:25.436
This is where it gets really interesting.

00:04:25.436 --> 00:04:26.836
(upbeat music)

00:04:26.836 --> 00:04:29.120
There are a few techniques
that the Dutch use

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.630
for their wizardry over the water.

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:33.980
The first one has to do
with them building a wall

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:37.113
around a body of water that
they want to turn into land.

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:42.070
Build a wall around it and
then they, back in the day,

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:44.990
would build a windmill next to those walls

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:48.160
and they would use the windmill to spin,

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:49.425
and as the windmill would spin,

00:04:49.425 --> 00:04:53.040
that would spin a pump that
would pump the water out

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:54.018
of that land.

00:04:54.018 --> 00:04:56.601
(upbeat music)

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:02.000
They'll plant on it,

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.870
and they will do whatever they need to do

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.170
to actually make it a
firm, dry, habitable land

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:10.153
and then they'll build entire cities on.

00:05:10.153 --> 00:05:12.736
(upbeat music)

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:26.999
And then in 1932, Holland had a huge win.

00:05:26.999 --> 00:05:29.666
(upbeat music)

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:33.000
There's this giant part of the country

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:36.200
that was a part of the sea.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.493
And they finally built this huge wall.

00:05:38.493 --> 00:05:41.076
(upbeat music)

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:48.913
Building this giant
wall, created a barrier

00:05:48.913 --> 00:05:53.913
between the saltwater sea and
made this huge body of water

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:56.427
into a fresh water lake.

00:05:56.427 --> 00:05:57.950
(upbeat music)

00:05:57.950 --> 00:05:59.610
After they built this wall,

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:02.120
they then started to
section off little pieces

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:04.170
of this newly created Lake,

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:07.140
and to start to turn
those into land as well.

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:10.570
So this is all of the land
that they have created

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:14.500
since 1932, when they built
a wall to make this Lake.

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:15.817
I mean, it's totally crazy.

00:06:15.817 --> 00:06:18.567
(dramatic music)

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:29.690
The Netherlands,
actually, a few years ago,

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:32.900
got a new province, like a
new state in their country,

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:35.330
not because of any administrative reform,

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:38.980
but because they literally
reclaimed a giant piece of land

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:40.891
that used to be under the sea.

00:06:40.891 --> 00:06:43.724
(dramatic music)

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:51.340
So much of the Dutch
coastline looks like this,

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:54.120
just super fortified with asphalt

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:56.530
and a million other building materials

00:06:56.530 --> 00:06:57.910
that they have come to

00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:01.290
for hundreds and hundreds
of years of experimentation.

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:03.620
It seems simple, it's like a wall,

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:07.690
but in this wall lies the big secret

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:10.920
to Holland not sinking,

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:12.700
and they don't always work.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:16.460
There have been times
when these walls break,

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:19.169
but for the most part, this
has been a success story,

00:07:19.169 --> 00:07:22.419
(soft uplifting music)

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:37.410
But it's not just
creating land out of water

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:40.710
it's also just how they manage water

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:42.182
in every one of their cities.

00:07:42.182 --> 00:07:45.599
(cheerful upbeat music)

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:52.950
Amsterdam used to just be, I mean,

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:54.960
you can hear it in the name, a dam

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.150
on the Amstel river.

00:07:56.150 --> 00:07:57.160
(cheerful upbeat music)

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:58.560
They then built it up

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:00.990
and they created this series of canals,

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:03.590
a very intentional design, as you can see,

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:04.423
and in doing so,

00:08:04.423 --> 00:08:08.300
they made this city a
very accessible boat city,

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:09.680
which was a very lucrative thing to do

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:12.600
back in like the 1500's and 1600's.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:15.470
Amsterdam became an economic hub in Europe

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:17.200
and developed a very quickly.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:21.460
A population boom contributed
to the golden age of Holland.

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:24.560
And even today, Amsterdam is a giant

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:26.890
economic and global hub,

00:08:26.890 --> 00:08:29.410
which you can attribute to how the Dutch

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:31.070
have just mastered water

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:34.770
and learned how to intentionally
design their cities

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:37.068
and their country around water management.

00:08:37.068 --> 00:08:40.401
(cheerful upbeat music)

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:47.390
A lot of the things we think
of as quintessential of Dutch

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:50.800
come from this culture
of water management.

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.670
And it now that sounds like the
wonkiest thing in the world,

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:55.730
but listen to me here, see the bikes,

00:08:55.730 --> 00:08:57.910
the bikes are a product of this low land

00:08:57.910 --> 00:09:00.110
because when you have flat land,

00:09:00.110 --> 00:09:01.280
it's relatively close together

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:03.950
because as most of the
land is waterlogged,

00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:05.750
then bikes become a really efficient,

00:09:05.750 --> 00:09:07.840
viable transportation means.

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:12.210
You also have some of the most
fertile grounds in the world

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:13.930
for growing grass,

00:09:13.930 --> 00:09:17.080
which then becomes
fertile pastures for cows,

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:19.630
which produce amazing dairy products,

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:24.350
which is why Dutch cheese is
such wonderful, amazing cheese.

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:26.150
And then of course there are windmills.

00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:27.990
Windmills are a huge Dutch thing.

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:31.760
Windmills come from this
history of pumping water

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:36.610
from lakes and the ocean to
create new pieces of land.

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:38.510
For a long time windmills
were the technology,

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:41.060
which is why Poland is full of windmills.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:42.890
Finally, you have these tulips.

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:45.800
Tulips are another huge Dutch thing.

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:47.370
The reason for this is that tulips grow

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:51.580
in this special clay-sand-soil mixture

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:55.500
and a lot of that exact soil
is right here in Holland

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:58.610
because of the fact
that a lot of this land

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:00.810
was under water before they reclaimed it,

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:03.460
and so it's perfect for growing tulips.

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:04.690
So a lot of Dutch culture

00:10:04.690 --> 00:10:07.540
could be attributed to water management

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:09.260
and conquering the water.

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:11.927
(upbeat music)

00:10:17.585 --> 00:10:19.750
I hope you now understand
why Amsterdam has canals

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:22.420
and the marvel of Dutch water management.

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:23.890
So much more to learn.

